  "rating": {
    "inherent": "low",
    "residual": "low",
    "forecast": "low",
    "rationale": "Manual validation applied. Reviewed prompt, tool manifest, and runtime notes. The design exposes only a read-only search over internal published policies and a reply channel bound to the authenticated requester. Structural controls sever broader exfiltration paths: replies are session-bound, the client does not auto-fetch content, and network egress is denied and reportedly pen-tested. No untrusted source reaches a sensitive sink today, and there are no write, execute, spend, delegate, config, or credential-access capabilities. Missing runtime details around logging and session assurance limit confidence on some STRIDE pairs, but they do not raise the present or forecast tier above low for this bounded Q&A design."
  },
